 "dates": "Tuesday, October 20 – Sunday, October 25, 2009",
 "logline": "Six friends, a borrowed minivan, Highway 1 and a monastery that sells fruitcake: the week everybody tries to behave.",
 "previously": [
  {
   "text": "On the beach Wes showed you a picture of a ring. Lena’s Mémère gave it to him at Easter. “Don’t say nothing to her.”",
   "if": "knows_wes_ring"
  },
  {
   "text": "At four in the morning, in a library stairwell, you told Lena the truth: you didn’t say yes. You drank, and Wes took it for one.",
   "if": "e10_cor_truth"
  },
  {
   "text": "At four in the morning, in a library stairwell: “Wes told me.”",
   "if": "!e10_cor_truth"
  },
  {
   "text": "“Wes doesn’t argue either. He says he out-waits me.”"
  },
  {
   "text": "At seven the bells woke her on your shoulder. You said her name. She looked at her phone.",
   "if": "e10_dawn==\"magdalena\""
  },
  {
   "text": "At seven the bells woke her on your shoulder. You didn’t move.",
   "if": "e10_dawn==\"still\""
  },
  {
   "text": "At seven the bells woke her on your shoulder. You told her what her face was doing.",
   "if": "e10_dawn==\"face\""
  },
  {
   "text": "In the middle of the midterm you heard what you’d said at dawn: “Aquinas and football. That’s the dream girl right there.”"
  },
  {
   "text": "Becca said you look at her like she’s homework. “Then do your homework, Jack. I’ll wait.” She tore off the list. “Due Halloween.”"
  }
 ],
